{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1705","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1705","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1705\",\"parent_revision\":\"da1f40a7aeef9919d6ec699a84887200431fd32a3bfde50d26e3e4ab271fa3ac\",\"root_revision\":\"da1f40a7aeef9919d6ec699a84887200431fd32a3bfde50d26e3e4ab271fa3ac\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe development harness grooming pipeline exhibits several observed workflow gaps and inefficiencies:\\n\\n1. `artifact_list` does not check that count > 0 before proceeding, which can cause downstream errors when the artifact list is empty.\\n2. The first groomer agent is blocked on `backlog_groom` under certain conditions (exact trigger conditions not captured in source).\\n3. The context manifest is being written to P001 (disk) rather than the expected destination (destination partially obscured in source).\\n4. Discovery and groom steps both perform overlapping collection work, producing duplicate effort.\\n\\nAdditionally, the RT-ICA gate, discovery gate, and staleness gate run sequentially for every item. For `status:groomed` items under 7 days old with no functional commits on impact files, all three checks require separate agent invocations rather than a single round-trip.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Screenshot of a session output showing a \\\"Gap observed\\\" section listing the four gaps above, followed by a structural proposal for a `preflight_check(issue_number, groomed_date)` MCP tool that would return `{rt_ica: \\\"APPROVED\\\", staleness: \\\"COSMETIC_ONLY\\\", feature_context: \\\"exists\\\"}` in one call, replacing three sequential agent invocations. User confirmed the abbreviation is \\\"MCP\\\" (not \\\"MVP\\\") improvements to the development harness.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **development harness grooming pipeline: sequential gate overhead and observed workflow gaps** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User report \u2014 screenshot of session output with observed gaps (2026-04-11)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-11\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0933901e20be212d2f3167f5a252e8a59c4af45b81300589713d97847b9967da\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVV9oQw\"}"}